{"The new getCredentials method accesses myUser.recoveryCodes and myUser.otp without first checking if myUser is null, while getMyUser(user) can return null when the user doesn't exist in storage": 0.8659171462059021, "The recoveryCodeCredentialProvider is fetched unconditionally at the start of the method but is only used in the else branch when userStorageCreated is false, causing unnecessary provider lookup when credentials are successfully created in user storage": 0.5316522717475891, "The enterRecoveryCodes helper method is copied verbatim from RecoveryAuthnCodesAuthenticatorTest.java, creating code duplication that increases maintenance burden and risks inconsistent bug fixes": 0.22279128432273865}